    "title": "Girls basketball: Fourth-quarter rally falls short for Chariho against Classical | Chariho High School Sports | thewesterlysun.com",
    "text": "PROVIDENCE — Menuhki Harris scored 11 points for Chariho in its 38-35 loss to Classical.\nThe Chargers (2-6) trailed by 14 points - 31-17 - heading into the fourth quarter and were down 38-28 with just over a minute remaining before making things interesting in the final minute.\nTrailing 38-28 - Chariho - behind three-point shots from Nora Downing and Adrianna Noka pulled within 38-35 and had an opportunity to tie the game with a three in the final seconds.\n\"I'm so proud of this team's fight,\" Chariho coach Dan LaBelle said. \"Down 14 going into the fourth we fought back and gave ourselves a chance to tie it down the stretch.\"\nDaniella Jimenez paced the Purple (1-2) with 18 points.\n— Rich Zalusky",
